Package: reduceTo
Title: Optimal Short-Form Scale Derivation
Version: 1.7.3
Authors@R:
    person("Paddy", "Maher", email = "paddycarstenmaher@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Finds the subset of items that makes the best short form of a
    scale: the one whose sum score correlates most strongly with the full
    scale, with an external criterion, or that best classifies a binary
    outcome (by Youden's J, the area under the ROC curve or a binarised
    correlation). Every combination of items is scored when that is feasible,
    by a parallel C++ engine that skips combinations which provably cannot
    reach the top; larger problems use a knockout search, which trims the
    scale, exhaustively searches the closest calls around the best short form
    found, and repeats the search with each of its items left out. Handles
    missing data, reverse-keyed items and cross-validation.
